nough target support to avoid excessive final scale-up while still exploring OAR sparing, conformity, and falloff.",\n    "Every proposed edit must pass geometry feasibility, target/OAR conflict, and expected final-normalization checks.",\n    "Target lower-bound objectives must remain compatible with target upper-bound objectives.",\n    "Avoid aggressive sub-prescription global upper-bound objectives for overlapping OARs or target-OAR interface helpers unless the structure_policy explicitly supports that use.",\n    "Separated OARs and outside-target rings may have sub-prescription upper-bound objectives when physically achievable.",\n    "Interface helpers should reduce excess hotspot, not force target-overlap tissue below prescription.",\n    "Geometry checks should shape the edit choice, not cause the planner to ignore a structure when another safe objective is available."\n  ],\n  "editing_rules": [\n    "For upper-bound objectives, tighter means lower DoseLevel, lower allowed volume, and/or higher Weight.",\n    "For lower-bound objectives, tighter means higher DoseLevel, higher required volume, and/or higher Weight.",\n    "DoseLevel and volume test the Pareto frontier; Weight controls how strongly the optimizer chases that objective.",\n    "Prefer meaningful bounded edits over tiny changes during early Pareto exploration.",\n    "Use larger edits mainly on primary target and true OAR objectives early.",\n    "Use smaller edits on rings and interface helpers, but still edit them when they support conformity, falloff, or hotspot control.",\n    "Use larger Weight escalation when an objective is clinically important, failing, repeatedly ineffective, or competing against many opposing objectives.",\n    "For persistent failures or local plateau, Weight changes up to one order of magnitude are allowed when consistent with guardrails.",\n    "Do not repeatedly edit only one or two structures when many structures have plausible safe Pareto headroom.",\n    "Late iterations should preserve hard-goal passing while still allowing small safe Pareto improvements."\n  ],\n  "clinical_priorities": [\n    "Clinical goals are the primary arbiter of final plan quality after prescription normalization.",\n    "Current pre-normalization target-min failures should not automatically suppress safe Pareto-headroom exploration because final normalization may improve target coverage while also increasing hotspots and OAR doses.",\n    "Maintain enough target support and hotspot control to make final normalization safe.",\n    "Meet required clinical goals whenever physically achievable after final normalization.",\n    "Improve OAR sparing, conformity, and falloff when bounded headroom exists and normalization risk is acceptable.",\n    "Prefer broad, coordinated Pareto improvement over narrow single-goal repair when safety gates allow it."\n  ]\n}\n\n## STRATEGIES\n{\n  "strategy_use_policy": [\n    "Use strategies to describe the clinical mechanism behind the proposed edits.",\n    "Select strategies that match the current clinical goals, objective behavior, structure role, and geometry context.",\n    "Multiple strategies may be selected when the proposal improves several Pareto fronts at once.",\n    "Do not select a strategy only because an objective has low FunctionValue; first check geometry, normalization risk, and clinical priority.",\n    "A failing hard goal should receive strong attention, but safe Pareto improvements on other structures may be pursued simultaneously."\n  ],\n  "strategies": [\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "support_target_coverage",\n      "when_to_use": "Target coverage is failing, fragile, or low enough that final normalization may excessively scale up hotspot and OAR dose.",\n      "objective_direction": "tighten_lower_bound"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "control_target_hotspot",\n      "when_to_use": "Target max dose, hotspot, or high-dose shape is failing, fragile, or likely to worsen after final normalization.",\n      "objective_direction": "tighten_upper_bound"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "reduce_true_oar_dose",\n      "when_to_use": "A true OAR clinical goal is failing, fragile, or has safe Pareto headroom after checking geometry and target robustness.",\n      "objective_direction": "tighten_upper_bound"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "reduce_interface_hotspot",\n      "when_to_use": "The dominant issue is localized high dose at a target-OAR interface or overlap-helper structure.",\n      "objective_direction": "tighten_upper_bound"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "improve_conformity",\n      "when_to_use": "The conformity index goal is failing or borderline, or prescription-dose spill near the target appears excessive.",\n      "objective_direction": "tighten_upper_bound"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "improve_falloff",\n      "when_to_use": "Mid-dose or low-dose spill can likely improve using ring objectives without compromising target coverage or OAR hard goals.",\n      "objective_direction": "tighten_upper_bound"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "relax_blocking_objective",\n      "when_to_use": "An upper-bound objective appears to be blocking a higher-priority target or clinical goal, especially when geometry makes the current constraint unrealistic.",\n      "objective_direction": "relax_upper_bound"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "explore_safe_pareto_headroom",\n      "when_to_use": "A passing goal or low-pressure objective has plausible remaining headroom, and tightening is safe after checking geometry, normalization, and higher-priority goals.",\n      "objective_direction": "case_dependent"\n    },\n    {\n      "strategy_name": "multi_front_pareto_exploration",\n      "when_to_use": "Multiple clinical fronts have failures, fragility, or safe headroom. Use coordinated edits across target, true OARs, helpers, and rings while respecting geometry and normalization risk.",\n      "objective_direction": "mixed"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## GUARDRAILS\n{\n  "max_selected_strategies": 10,\n  "max_total_actions": 25,\n  "max_structure_actions": 3,\n  "max_objective_actions": 25,\n  "max_new_helper_structures": 3,\n  "change_limits": {\n    "weight_change_ratio": {\n      "min": 0.1,\n      "max": 10.0\n    },\n    "dose_change_cgy": {\n      "max": 1000.0\n    },\n    "volume_change_percent": {\n      "max": 25.0\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n## OUTPUT SCHEMA SUMMARY\n{\n  "allowed": {\n    "objective_actions": [\n      "modify"\n    ],\n    "objective_function_types": [\n      "MinDose",\n      "MaxDose",\n      "MinDvh",\n      "MaxDvh"\n    ],\n    "hypothesis_result_values": [\n      "supported",\n      "partly_supported",\n      "unsupported",\n      "contradicted",\n      "baseline_template"\n    ],\n    "restart_decision_values": [\n      "restart",\n      "continue_without_restart"\n    ]\n  },\n  "numeric_limits": {\n    "Weight": {\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 500.0\n    },\n    "DoseLevel": {\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 100000.0\n    },\n    "PercentVolume": {\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 100.0\n    },\n    "AbsoluteVolume": {\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 100000.0\n    }\n  },\n  "field_rules": {\n    "roi_name": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    },\n    "objective_index": {\n      "type": "int",\n      "min": 0\n    },\n    "FunctionType": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false,\n      "allowed_values": [\n        "MinDose",\n        "MaxDose",\n        "MinDvh",\n        "MaxDvh"\n      ]\n    },\n    "Weight": {\n      "type": [\n        "int",\n        "float",\n        "none"\n      ],\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 500.0\n    },\n    "DoseLevel": {\n      "type": [\n        "int",\n        "float",\n        "none"\n      ],\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 100000.0\n    },\n    "PercentVolume": {\n      "type": [\n        "int",\n        "float",\n        "none"\n      ],\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 100.0\n    },\n    "AbsoluteVolume": {\n      "type": [\n        "int",\n        "float",\n        "none"\n      ],\n      "min": 0.0,\n      "max": 100000.0\n    },\n    "strategy_name": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    },\n    "reason": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    },\n    "iteration": {\n      "type": "int",\n      "min": 0\n    },\n    "hypothesis": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    },\n    "action_summary": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    },\n    "observed_effect": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    },\n    "observed_outcome_summary": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    },\n    "hypothesis_result": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false,\n      "allowed_values": [\n        "supported",\n        "partly_supported",\n        "unsupported",\n        "contradicted",\n        "baseline_template"\n      ]\n    },\n    "restart_decision": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false,\n      "allowed_values": [\n        "restart",\n        "continue_without_restart"\n      ]\n    },\n    "restart_reason": {\n      "type": "str",\n      "allow_empty": false\n    }\n  },\n  "objective_modify_parameter_keys": [\n    "Weight",\n    "DoseLevel",\n    "PercentVolume",\n    "AbsoluteVolume"\n  ],\n  "objective_required_base_fields": [\n    "Weight",\n    "DoseLevel"\n  ],\n  "prompt_metadata": {\n    "dvh_rule": "For MinDvh and MaxDvh, include exactly one volume field: PercentVolume or AbsoluteVolume.",\n    "change_format_rule": "In objectives.modify[*].changes, include only parameters that should actually change. Do not include null fields. Do not include PercentVolume or AbsoluteVolume unless changing a DVH objective volume parameter.",\n    "lower_upper_dose_order_rule": "For the same ROI, every lower-bound objective DoseLevel (MinDose or MinDvh) must be less than every upper-bound objective DoseLevel (MaxDose or MaxDvh). Do not propose target minimum/lower-bound doses that are greater than or equal to target maximum/upper-bound doses.",\n    "objective_parameter_examples": [\n      {\n        "FunctionType": "MinDose",\n        "DoseLevel": 4400.0,\n        "Weight": 100.0\n      },\n      {\n        "FunctionType": "MaxDose",\n        "DoseLevel": 4500.0,\n        "Weight": 40.0\n      },\n      {\n        "FunctionType": "MinDvh",\n        "DoseLevel": 4500.0,\n        "PercentVolume": 97.0,\n        "Weight": 20.0\n      },\n      {\n        "FunctionType": "MaxDvh",\n        "DoseLevel": 3700.0,\n        "PercentVolume": 20.0,\n        "Weight": 10.0\n      },\n      {\n        "FunctionType": "MaxDvh",\n        "DoseLevel": 4500.0,\n        "AbsoluteVolume": 195.0,\n        "Weight": 1.0\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  "selected_strategies": {\n    "type": "list",\n    "required_item_keys": [\n      "strategy_name",\n      "reason"\n    ],\n    "allow_unknown_item_keys": false\n  },\n  "objectives": {\n    "required_action_keys": [\n      "modify"\n    ],\n    "allow_unknown_action_keys": false,\n    "actions": {\n      "modify": {\n        "required_fields": [\n          "roi_name",\n          "objective_index",\n          "changes"\n        ],\n        "optional_fields": [],\n        "allow_unknown_fields": false,\n        "drop_invalid_items": true,\n        "allowed_change_keys": [\n          "Weight",\n          "DoseLevel",\n          "PercentVolume",\n          "AbsoluteVolume"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  "review_previous_iteration": {\n    "type": "dict",\n    "required_keys": [\n      "iteration",\n      "observed_outcome_summary",\n      "strategy_action_outcomes",\n      "hypothesis_result"\n    ],\n    "allow_unknown_keys": false,\n    "strategy_action_outcomes": {\n      "type": "list",\n      "required_item_keys": [\n        "strategy_name",\n        "observed_effect"\n      ],\n      "allow_unknown_item_keys": false\n    }\n  },\n  "propose_next_iteration": {\n    "type": "dict",\n    "required_keys": [\n      "iteration",\n      "hypothesis",\n      "strategy_actions"\n    ],\n    "optional_keys": [\n      "restart_decision",\n      "restart_reason"\n    ],\n    "allow_unknown_keys": false,\n    "strategy_actions": {\n      "type": "list",\n      "required_item_keys": [\n        "strategy_name",\n        "reason",\n        "action_summary"\n      ],\n      "allow_unknown_item_keys": false\n    }\n  },\n  "restart": {\n    "restart_decision_values": [\n      "restart",\n      "continue_without_restart"\n    ]\n  },\n  "response": {\n    "required_top_level_keys": [\n      "selected_strategies",\n      "objectives",\n      "review_previous_iteration",\n      "propose_next_iteration",\n      "restart_decision",\n      "restart_reason"\n    ],\n    "allow_unknown_top_level_keys": false\n  },\n  "response_template": {\n    "selected_strategies": [\n      {\n        "strategy_name": "reduce_oar_dose",\n        "reason": "Selected because the current state supports bounded upper-bound tightening."\n      }\n    ],\n    "objectives": {\n      "modify": [\n        {\n          "roi_name": "Example ROI Name",\n          "objective_index": 0,\n          "changes": {\n            "DoseLevel": 3700.0,\n            "Weight": 20.0\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "review_previous_iteration": {\n      "iteration": 0,\n      "observed_outcome_summary": "",\n      "strategy_action_outcomes": [\n        {\n          "strategy_name": "",\n          "observed_effect": ""\n        }\n      ],\n      "hypothesis_result": ""\n    },\n    "propose_next_iteration": {\n      "iteration": 1,\n      "hypothesis": "",\n      "strategy_actions": [\n        {\n          "strategy_name": "",\n          "reason": "",\n          "action_summary": ""\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    "restart_decision": "continue_without_restart",\n    "restart_reason": ""\n  }\n}\n\n## STRUCTURE POLICY\n{\n  "policy_name": "male_pelvis_structure_policy",\n  "site": "male_pelvis",\n  "general_rules": [\n    "Use the structure-specific default_geometry_assumption as the planning geometry context.",\n    "Do not infer geometric overlap, separation, or adjacency from objective values or clinical goal values alone.",\n    "Do not treat all OAR upper-bound objectives the same; separated OARs, overlapping OARs, and interface helpers have different feasible dose behavior.",\n    "For structures assumed to overlap or directly interface with target, keep MaxDose objectives above prescription unless explicitly justified by the policy.",\n    "Use interface helpers to reduce excess target-OAR interface hotspot, not to create cold dose regions at the target interface.",\n    "Use rings primarily for conformity and falloff shaping, not as substitutes for target or true OAR objectives."\n  ],\n  "structure_geometry": {\n    "PTV4500": {\n      "geometry_role": "target",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "primary_prescription_target",\n      "planning_role": "Primary prescription target and final normalization structure.",\n      "contains_or_expands_from": [\n        "CTV4500"\n      ],\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Maintain coverage, robustness, and clinically sensible dose shape.",\n        "Target lower-bound objectives must remain compatible with target upper-bound objectives.",\n        "When competing OAR, helper, or ring objectives are tightened, preserve enough target support to avoid excessive final normalization scale-up."\n      ]\n    },\n    "CTV4500": {\n      "geometry_role": "nested_target",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "inside_or_closely_related_to_ptv",\n      "planning_role": "Clinical target volume inside or closely related to PTV4500.",\n      "inside_or_related_to": "PTV4500",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Coverage support is important when CTV coverage is failing or fragile.",\n        "Do not push CTV lower-bound DoseLevel above relevant PTV upper-bound DoseLevel.",\n        "Coordinate CTV coverage support with PTV hotspot control so target objectives do not become internally contradictory."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Bladder": {\n      "geometry_role": "overlapping_oar",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "overlaps_or_directly_interfaces_with_ptv",\n      "overlaps_target": true,\n      "planning_role": "True OAR assumed to overlap or directly interface with PTV4500.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Prefer DVH-volume sparing and interface-helper control over global sub-prescription MaxDose.",\n        "Avoid tightening global MaxDose below prescription because target-overlap tissue may need prescription dose.",\n        "If bladder max dose is failing, reduce excess hotspot without creating a target coverage conflict.",\n        "Safe bladder sparing can still be pursued aggressively through DVH objectives when target robustness is maintained."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Rectum": {\n      "geometry_role": "overlapping_oar",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "overlaps_or_directly_interfaces_with_ptv",\n      "overlaps_target": true,\n      "planning_role": "True OAR assumed to overlap or directly interface with PTV4500.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Prefer DVH-volume sparing and interface-helper control over global sub-prescription MaxDose.",\n        "Avoid tightening global MaxDose below prescription because target-overlap tissue may need prescription dose.",\n        "Continue safe DVH sparing when rectum goals have Pareto headroom and target robustness is maintained."\n      ]\n    },\n    "SmallBowel": {\n      "geometry_role": "case_dependent_oar",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "unknown_or_case_dependent_relationship_to_ptv",\n      "overlaps_target": "unknown_or_case_dependent",\n      "planning_role": "True OAR whose spatial relationship to PTV may vary by patient.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use current clinical goals and objective behavior to decide whether bowel sparing has safe headroom.",\n        "Sub-prescription DVH objectives may be reasonable, but avoid aggressive hotspot suppression that could conflict with target coverage.",\n        "If bowel max dose is failing, consider whether an associated interface helper or high-dose objective should control excess hotspot."\n      ]\n    },\n    "LargeBowel": {\n      "geometry_role": "case_dependent_oar",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "unknown_or_case_dependent_relationship_to_ptv",\n      "overlaps_target": "unknown_or_case_dependent",\n      "planning_role": "True OAR whose spatial relationship to PTV may vary by patient.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use current clinical goals and objective behavior to decide whether bowel sparing has safe headroom.",\n        "Sub-prescription DVH objectives may be reasonable, but avoid aggressive hotspot suppression that could conflict with target coverage.",\n        "If bowel max dose is failing, consider whether an associated interface helper or high-dose objective should control excess hotspot."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Femur_Head_R": {\n      "geometry_role": "separated_oar",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "usually_separated_from_high_dose_target",\n      "overlaps_target": false,\n      "planning_role": "True OAR usually spatially separated from the high-dose target.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Sub-prescription upper-bound objectives may be reasonable when physically achievable.",\n        "Safe Pareto tightening is allowed, but do not over-prioritize if dose is already very low and not clinically limiting."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Femur_Head_L": {\n      "geometry_role": "separated_oar",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "usually_separated_from_high_dose_target",\n      "overlaps_target": false,\n      "planning_role": "True OAR usually spatially separated from the high-dose target.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Sub-prescription upper-bound objectives may be reasonable when physically achievable.",\n        "Safe Pareto tightening is allowed, but do not over-prioritize if dose is already very low and not clinically limiting."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Ring03mm": {\n      "geometry_role": "near_target_ring",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "outside_target_near_prescription_ring",\n      "planning_role": "Near-target conformity and prescription-dose spill control. This is the primary shaping structure for improving the conformity index clinical goal around PTV4500.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use Ring03mm as the primary near-target conformity and prescription-dose spill control structure.",\n        "Ring03mm MaxDose should usually stay at prescription dose or below, especially when conformity is failing, borderline, or close to threshold.",\n        "Do not relax Ring03mm above prescription just to recover PTV coverage unless this is an explicit clinical trade-off with no safer deblocking option."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Ring15mm": {\n      "geometry_role": "falloff_ring",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "outside_target_mid_distance_falloff_ring",\n      "planning_role": "Mid-distance dose falloff control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use for mid-dose conformity and falloff.",\n        "Sub-prescription objectives are usually appropriate because the ring is assumed outside target.",\n        "Avoid repeated escalation unless falloff remains a dominant problem."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Ring30mm": {\n      "geometry_role": "falloff_ring",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "outside_target_low_dose_falloff_ring",\n      "planning_role": "Low-dose bath and distant falloff control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use for low-dose falloff.",\n        "Sub-prescription objectives are appropriate because the ring is assumed outside target.",\n        "Avoid over-weighting if target or OAR hard goals are more limiting."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Blad Opt": {\n      "geometry_role": "target_oar_interface_helper",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "target_adjacent_or_potential_target_overlap_helper",\n      "associated_oar": "Bladder",\n      "planning_role": "PTV-Bladder interface helper for localized high-dose control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Assume this helper is target-adjacent or may include target-overlap interface tissue.",\n        "Use it to reduce excess interface hotspot, not to create a cold region at the PTV-Bladder interface.",\n        "Avoid pushing MaxDose well below prescription because this may compete with target coverage.",\n        "If lowering DoseLevel below prescription is considered, it should be modest, clearly justified by current plan evidence, and coordinated with target coverage support.",\n        "When target coverage is failing or fragile, prefer keeping this helper near prescription rather than aggressively below prescription."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Rec Opt": {\n      "geometry_role": "target_oar_interface_helper",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "target_adjacent_or_potential_target_overlap_helper",\n      "associated_oar": "Rectum",\n      "planning_role": "PTV-Rectum interface helper for localized high-dose control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Assume this helper is target-adjacent or may include target-overlap interface tissue.",\n        "Use it to reduce excess interface hotspot, not to create a cold region at the PTV-Rectum interface.",\n        "Avoid pushing MaxDose well below prescription because this may compete with target coverage.",\n        "If lowering DoseLevel below prescription is considered, it should be modest, clearly justified by current plan evidence, and coordinated with target coverage support.",\n        "When target coverage is failing or fragile, prefer keeping this helper near prescription rather than aggressively below prescription."\n      ]\n    },\n    "SB Opt": {\n      "geometry_role": "target_oar_interface_helper",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "case_dependent_target_adjacent_helper",\n      "associated_oar": "SmallBowel",\n      "planning_role": "PTV-SmallBowel interface helper for localized high-dose control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Assume this helper may be target-adjacent unless patient-specific geometry says otherwise.",\n        "Use it to reduce excess interface hotspot.",\n        "Avoid pushing MaxDose well below prescription when target coverage is failing or fragile.",\n        "Sub-prescription MaxDose may be reasonable only if the helper is intended as outside-target falloff control.",\n        "Without explicit geometry, prefer modest changes near prescription rather than aggressive sub-prescription tightening."\n      ]\n    },\n    "LB Opt": {\n      "geometry_role": "target_oar_interface_helper",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "case_dependent_target_adjacent_helper",\n      "associated_oar": "LargeBowel",\n      "planning_role": "PTV-LargeBowel interface helper for localized high-dose control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Assume this helper may be target-adjacent unless patient-specific geometry says otherwise.",\n        "Use it to reduce excess interface hotspot.",\n        "Avoid pushing MaxDose well below prescription when target coverage is failing or fragile.",\n        "Sub-prescription MaxDose may be reasonable only if the helper is intended as outside-target falloff control.",\n        "Without explicit geometry, prefer modest changes near prescription rather than aggressive sub-prescription tightening."\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n## MEMORY POLICY\n{\n  "name": "iteration_review_and_memory_policy",\n  "goal": "Use prior_iterations_context as explicit iteration memory. Review the most recent completed optimizer result before proposing the next bounded optimizer edit.",\n  "memory_model": [\n    "prior_iterations_context.history contains one record per optimizer iteration.",\n    "Each record may contain selected_strategies, which stores the high-level planning strategies selected for that iteration.",\n    "Each record may contain a propose_next_iteration block, which stores the hypothesis and strategy_actions proposed for that iteration.",\n    "Each record may contain a review_previous_iteration block, which stores the observed outcome after that iteration has been optimized.",\n    "The record whose iteration equals review_previous_iteration.iteration is the record being reviewed.",\n    "The record whose iteration equals propose_next_iteration.iteration is the proposal being evaluated by the next optimizer run.",\n    "A newly proposed record contains selected_strategies and propose_next_iteration; it does not yet contain observed outcome evidence for itself.",\n    "Earlier records that already contain review_previous_iteration are completed memory and should be used as background evidence.",\n    "The memory file stores semantic planning memory, not raw objective edits or executable proposal details."\n  ],\n  "review_previous_iteration_rules": [\n    "Use the current optimization_state to evaluate the most recent proposed iteration that now has an optimizer result.",\n    "Fill review_previous_iteration for the reviewed iteration only.",\n    "Fill observed_outcome_summary, strategy_action_outcomes.observed_effect, and hypothesis_result using actual current plan evidence.",\n    "Do not rewrite the reviewed iteration\'s prior selected_strategies, hypothesis, strategy reasons, or action summaries.",\n    "Base observed outcomes on actual optimized plan behavior, not on the expected effect of the prior proposal.",\n    "Use hypothesis_result only as supported, partly_supported, unsupported, contradicted, or baseline_template.",\n    "Use baseline_template only for the deterministic iteration 0 template baseline entry."\n  ],\n  "propose_next_iteration_rules": [\n    "After reviewing the previous optimizer result, propose the next optimizer iteration.",\n    "The next proposal must include selected_strategies and a forward-looking propose_next_iteration block.",\n    "The propose_next_iteration block must include a hypothesis and strategy_actions.",\n    "Each selected_strategies item must include strategy_name and reason.",\n    "Each strategy_actions item must include strategy_name, reason, and action_summary.",\n    "The next proposal must not include observed outcomes for itself because it has not been optimized yet.",\n    "The next proposal becomes a new history record after Python applies and saves it.",\n    "The new history record should store selected_strategies and propose_next_iteration so future reviews can connect strategy choice, intended action, and observed effect.",\n    "The semantic strategy_actions.action_summary should summarize the intended objective-edit direction without storing raw objective edits."\n  ],\n  "adaptation_rules": [\n    "Use completed memory plus the newly reviewed previous iteration to avoid blindly repeating ineffective move patterns.",\n    "Continue or refine strategies that produced useful improvements without higher-priority regression.",\n    "If a prior strategy produced mixed tradeoffs, preserve the gain and make the next move more focused.",\n    "If a prior strategy caused regression, plateau, or little benefit, change strategy, objective choice, direction, or magnitude rather than repeating it.",\n    "If the same strategy has been repeated for several iterations with persistent failures or minimal qualitative improvement, explicitly adapt the next move instead of repeating the same rationale.",\n    "Use memory to explain why the next proposal is continuing, refining, reducing, or changing the prior strategy pattern.",\n    "Do not mark a hypothesis as supported solely because objective pressure increased or some intermediate values improved.",\n    "If the same clinical goals remain failing after the proposed strategy, use partly_supported unless the improvement is clearly clinically meaningful.",\n    "If the same strategy pattern has been repeated for 2 or more iterations and the same goals remain failing or borderline, describe this as possible plateau or diminishing return.",\n    "If objective edits are repeatedly tightening the same objectives with similar rationale, explicitly note repetition even if small improvements occurred.",\n    "Do not repeatedly tighten the same ring, helper, or overlapping-OAR objective in consecutive iterations unless the current optimized state shows it remains a dominant problem or the prior tightening clearly improved plan quality without target regression.",\n    "When target coverage remains failing or fragile, repeated tightening of rings, interface helpers, or overlapping OARs must be coordinated with stronger target support.",\n    "If a ring, helper, or overlapping-OAR objective was tightened in the prior iteration and the related clinical goal is now passing or improving, consider shifting the next edit to another Pareto front instead of tightening the same objective again.",\n    "If the same objective family is tightened repeatedly, explicitly explain whether the prior result supports continued pressure, reduced pressure, or a change in strategy.",\n    "When target coverage remains the dominant unresolved failure after broad Pareto exploration, prioritize stronger target support, a different target-support mechanism, or restart consideration over further ring/helper escalation.If broad multi-front edits improve OARs, rings, or helpers while target coverage remains failing, classify the outcome as mixed rather than fully supported.When memory identifies a focused dominant failure, do not abandon safe zero-value objective exploration. Preserve broad Pareto probing by editing zero-value objectives that are clinically relevant and unlikely to compete with the dominant repair.If zero-value objectives are skipped during a focused refinement iteration, explicitly explain why each skipped objective family was unsafe, redundant, or low clinical value."\n  ]\n}\n\n## RESTART POLICY\n{\n  "name": "memory_conditioned_pareto_restart_policy",\n  "minimum_optimization_runs_left_for_restart": 5,\n  "goal": "Use memory to decide when RayStation should restart from fluence so the optimizer can re-solve the deliverable MLC/MU pattern using the current learned objective settings.",\n  "restart_definition": "A restart deletes the current optimized MLC pattern and MU values, then starts optimization from fluence using the current objective values. It can escape a deliverable local minimum or test a new Pareto trajectory without adding optimization budget.",\n  "eligibility_rules": [\n    "remaining_runs = optimization_state.total_iterations - optimization_state.iteration + 1.",\n    "Restart is eligible only when remaining_runs >= 5.",\n    "If too few runs remain, choose continue_without_restart and fine tune locally."\n  ],\n  "good_restart_policy": [\n    "A good restart re-solves from fluence using the best learned objective set so far, not a reset to broad exploration from scratch.",\n    "Before restarting, preserve objective pressures that protected passing or near-threshold clinical fronts unless memory shows they caused a higher-priority failure.",\n    "Do not pair restart with broad relaxation of objectives responsible for target hotspot, OAR, conformity, or falloff safety.",\n    "If a prior restart was harmful, any later restart should use a corrected objective set that explicitly protects the fronts that failed after that restart."\n  ],\n  "decision_policy": [\n    "In the llm_memory_restart arm, at least one restart is strongly preferred while eligible once memory contains useful objective-setting knowledge.",\n    "Strongly consider the first restart after at least two completed LLM-guided iterations.",\n    "Prefer restart when memory shows plateau, regression, repeated ineffective local edits, persistent target/OAR tradeoff tension, suspected MLC/MU local-minimum behavior, or a learned objective set worth re-solving from fluence.",\n    "Restart should target deliverable Pareto improvement across coverage, hotspot control, OAR sparing, conformity, and falloff; do not restart only to chase intermediate prescription coverage.",\n    "Continue locally when the current trajectory is clearly improving, the next edit has a distinct mechanism, and enough eligible iterations remain to restart later.",\n    "After a harmful restart, usually try one clearly different local corrective iteration before considering another restart.",\n    "More than one restart is allowed when memory supports it; a harmful prior restart requires a clearer corrected objective rationale, not a permanent restart ban."\n  ],\n  "restart_check": [\n    "Check prior_iterations_context.history for previous restart_decision values and restart outcomes.",\n    "Check remaining_runs before choosing restart.",\n    "If no restart has been used and restart is eligible, give restart strong preference and explicitly justify any deferral.",\n    "If a restart has already been used, additional restarts remain available but must be justified by plateau, regression, persistent tradeoff tension, repeated ineffective local edits, or a corrected learned objective set."\n  ],\n  "output_rules": [\n    "Return restart_decision as \'restart\' or \'continue_without_restart\'.",\n    "If restarting, explain the memory evidence and identify which already-good clinical fronts the learned objective set is preserving.",\n    "If continuing without restart while eligible, explain why local continuation is preferred despite restart being strongly preferred in this arm."\n  ]\n}\n\n## OUTPUT CONTRACT\nReturn JSON only. Use the required top-level keys and action shapes from the output schema summary. Do not include keys outside the allowed response shape.', 'input': 'Return one valid JSON object only. Follow the output schema summary and output contract exactly. Use optimization_state.structures[*].dose_objectives only for editable objective parameters. Use optimization_state.