tightening is allowed, but do not over-prioritize if dose is already very low and not clinically limiting."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Ring03mm": {\n      "geometry_role": "near_target_ring",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "outside_target_near_prescription_ring",\n      "planning_role": "Near-target conformity and prescription-dose spill control. This is the primary shaping structure for improving the conformity index clinical goal around PTV4500.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use Ring03mm as the primary near-target conformity and prescription-dose spill control structure.",\n        "Ring03mm MaxDose should usually stay at prescription dose or below, especially when conformity is failing, borderline, or close to threshold.",\n        "Do not relax Ring03mm above prescription just to recover PTV coverage unless this is an explicit clinical trade-off with no safer deblocking option."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Ring15mm": {\n      "geometry_role": "falloff_ring",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "outside_target_mid_distance_falloff_ring",\n      "planning_role": "Mid-distance dose falloff control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use for mid-dose conformity and falloff.",\n        "Sub-prescription objectives are usually appropriate because the ring is assumed outside target.",\n        "Avoid repeated escalation unless falloff remains a dominant problem."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Ring30mm": {\n      "geometry_role": "falloff_ring",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "outside_target_low_dose_falloff_ring",\n      "planning_role": "Low-dose bath and distant falloff control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Use for low-dose falloff.",\n        "Sub-prescription objectives are appropriate because the ring is assumed outside target.",\n        "Avoid over-weighting if target or OAR hard goals are more limiting."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Blad Opt": {\n      "geometry_role": "target_oar_interface_helper",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "target_adjacent_or_potential_target_overlap_helper",\n      "associated_oar": "Bladder",\n      "planning_role": "PTV-Bladder interface helper for localized high-dose control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Assume this helper is target-adjacent or may include target-overlap interface tissue.",\n        "Use it to reduce excess interface hotspot, not to create a cold region at the PTV-Bladder interface.",\n        "Avoid pushing MaxDose well below prescription because this may compete with target coverage.",\n        "If lowering DoseLevel below prescription is considered, it should be modest, clearly justified by current plan evidence, and coordinated with target coverage support.",\n        "When target coverage is failing or fragile, prefer keeping this helper near prescription rather than aggressively below prescription."\n      ]\n    },\n    "Rec Opt": {\n      "geometry_role": "target_oar_interface_helper",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "target_adjacent_or_potential_target_overlap_helper",\n      "associated_oar": "Rectum",\n      "planning_role": "PTV-Rectum interface helper for localized high-dose control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Assume this helper is target-adjacent or may include target-overlap interface tissue.",\n        "Use it to reduce excess interface hotspot, not to create a cold region at the PTV-Rectum interface.",\n        "Avoid pushing MaxDose well below prescription because this may compete with target coverage.",\n        "If lowering DoseLevel below prescription is considered, it should be modest, clearly justified by current plan evidence, and coordinated with target coverage support.",\n        "When target coverage is failing or fragile, prefer keeping this helper near prescription rather than aggressively below prescription."\n      ]\n    },\n    "LB Opt": {\n      "geometry_role": "target_oar_interface_helper",\n      "default_geometry_assumption": "case_dependent_target_adjacent_helper",\n      "associated_oar": "LargeBowel",\n      "planning_role": "PTV-LargeBowel interface helper for localized high-dose control.",\n      "planning_notes": [\n        "Assume this helper may be target-adjacent unless patient-specific geometry says otherwise.",\n        "Use it to reduce excess interface hotspot.",\n        "Avoid pushing MaxDose well below prescription when target coverage is failing or fragile.",\n        "Sub-prescription MaxDose may be reasonable only if the helper is intended as outside-target falloff control.",\n        "Without explicit geometry, prefer modest changes near prescription rather than aggressive sub-prescription tightening."\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n## MEMORY POLICY\n{\n  "name": "iteration_review_and_memory_policy",\n  "goal": "Use prior_iterations_context as explicit iteration memory. Review the most recent completed optimizer result before proposing the next bounded optimizer edit.",\n  "memory_model": [\n    "prior_iterations_context.history contains one record per optimizer iteration.",\n    "Each record may contain selected_strategies, which stores the high-level planning strategies selected for that iteration.",\n    "Each record may contain a propose_next_iteration block, which stores the hypothesis and strategy_actions proposed for that iteration.",\n    "Each record may contain a review_previous_iteration block, which stores the observed outcome after that iteration has been optimized.",\n    "The record whose iteration equals review_previous_iteration.iteration is the record being reviewed.",\n    "The record whose iteration equals propose_next_iteration.iteration is the proposal being evaluated by the next optimizer run.",\n    "A newly proposed record contains selected_strategies and propose_next_iteration; it does not yet contain observed outcome evidence for itself.",\n    "Earlier records that already contain review_previous_iteration are completed memory and should be used as background evidence.",\n    "The memory file stores semantic planning memory, not raw objective edits or executable proposal details."\n  ],\n  "review_previous_iteration_rules": [\n    "Use the current optimization_state to evaluate the most recent proposed iteration that now has an optimizer result.",\n    "Fill review_previous_iteration for the reviewed iteration only.",\n    "Fill observed_outcome_summary, strategy_action_outcomes.observed_effect, and hypothesis_result using actual current plan evidence.",\n    "Do not rewrite the reviewed iteration\'s prior selected_strategies, hypothesis, strategy reasons, or action summaries.",\n    "Base observed outcomes on actual optimized plan behavior, not on the expected effect of the prior proposal.",\n    "Use hypothesis_result only as supported, partly_supported, unsupported, contradicted, or baseline_template.",\n    "Use baseline_template only for the deterministic iteration 0 template baseline entry."\n  ],\n  "propose_next_iteration_rules": [\n    "After reviewing the previous optimizer result, propose the next optimizer iteration.",\n    "The next proposal must include selected_strategies and a forward-looking propose_next_iteration block.",\n    "The propose_next_iteration block must include a hypothesis and strategy_actions.",\n    "Each selected_strategies item must include strategy_name and reason.",\n    "Each strategy_actions item must include strategy_name, reason, and action_summary.",\n    "The next proposal must not include observed outcomes for itself because it has not been optimized yet.",\n    "The next proposal becomes a new history record after Python applies and saves it.",\n    "The new history record should store selected_strategies and propose_next_iteration so future reviews can connect strategy choice, intended action, and observed effect.",\n    "The semantic strategy_actions.action_summary should summarize the intended objective-edit direction without storing raw objective edits."\n  ],\n  "adaptation_rules": [\n    "Use completed memory plus the newly reviewed previous iteration to avoid blindly repeating ineffective move patterns.",\n    "Continue or refine strategies that produced useful improvements without higher-priority regression.",\n    "If a prior strategy produced mixed tradeoffs, preserve the gain and make the next move more focused.",\n    "If a prior strategy caused regression, plateau, or little benefit, change strategy, objective choice, direction, or magnitude rather than repeating it.",\n    "If the same strategy has been repeated for several iterations with persistent failures or minimal qualitative improvement, explicitly adapt the next move instead of repeating the same rationale.",\n    "Use memory to explain why the next proposal is continuing, refining, reducing, or changing the prior strategy pattern.",\n    "Do not mark a hypothesis as supported solely because objective pressure increased or some intermediate values improved.",\n    "If the same clinical goals remain failing after the proposed strategy, use partly_supported unless the improvement is clearly clinically meaningful.",\n    "If the same strategy pattern has been repeated for 2 or more iterations and the same goals remain failing or borderline, describe this as possible plateau or diminishing return.",\n    "If objective edits are repeatedly tightening the same objectives with similar rationale, explicitly note repetition even if small improvements occurred.",\n    "Do not repeatedly tighten the same ring, helper, or overlapping-OAR objective in consecutive iterations unless the current optimized state shows it remains a dominant problem or the prior tightening clearly improved plan quality without target regression.",\n    "When target coverage remains failing or fragile, repeated tightening of rings, interface helpers, or overlapping OARs must be coordinated with stronger target support.",\n    "If a ring, helper, or overlapping-OAR objective was tightened in the prior iteration and the related clinical goal is now passing or improving, consider shifting the next edit to another Pareto front instead of tightening the same objective again.",\n    "If the same objective family is tightened repeatedly, explicitly explain whether the prior result supports continued pressure, reduced pressure, or a change in strategy.",\n    "When target coverage remains the dominant unresolved failure after broad Pareto exploration, prioritize stronger target support, a different target-support mechanism, or restart consideration over further ring/helper escalation.If broad multi-front edits improve OARs, rings, or helpers while target coverage remains failing, classify the outcome as mixed rather than fully supported.When memory identifies a focused dominant failure, do not abandon safe zero-value objective exploration. Preserve broad Pareto probing by editing zero-value objectives that are clinically relevant and unlikely to compete with the dominant repair.If zero-value objectives are skipped during a focused refinement iteration, explicitly explain why each skipped objective family was unsafe, redundant, or low clinical value."\n  ]\n}\n\n## RESTART POLICY\n{\n  "name": "memory_conditioned_pareto_restart_policy",\n  "minimum_optimization_runs_left_for_restart": 5,\n  "goal": "Use memory to decide when RayStation should restart from fluence so the optimizer can re-solve the deliverable MLC/MU pattern using the current learned objective settings.",\n  "restart_definition": "A restart deletes the current optimized MLC pattern and MU values, then starts optimization from fluence using the current objective values. It can escape a deliverable local minimum or test a new Pareto trajectory without adding optimization budget.",\n  "eligibility_rules": [\n    "remaining_runs = optimization_state.total_iterations - optimization_state.iteration + 1.",\n    "Restart is eligible only when remaining_runs >= 5.",\n    "If too few runs remain, choose continue_without_restart and fine tune locally."\n  ],\n  "good_restart_policy": [\n    "A good restart re-solves from fluence using the best learned objective set so far, not a reset to broad exploration from scratch.",\n    "Before restarting, preserve objective pressures that protected passing or near-threshold clinical fronts unless memory shows they caused a higher-priority failure.",\n    "Do not pair restart with broad relaxation of objectives responsible for target hotspot, OAR, conformity, or falloff safety.",\n    "If a prior restart was harmful, any later restart should use a corrected objective set that explicitly protects the fronts that failed after that restart."\n  ],\n  "decision_policy": [\n    "In the llm_memory_restart arm, at least one restart is strongly preferred while eligible once memory contains useful objective-setting knowledge.",\n    "Strongly consider the first restart after at least two completed LLM-guided iterations.",\n    "Prefer restart when memory shows plateau, regression, repeated ineffective local edits, persistent target/OAR tradeoff tension, suspected MLC/MU local-minimum behavior, or a learned objective set worth re-solving from fluence.",\n    "Restart should target deliverable Pareto improvement across coverage, hotspot control, OAR sparing, conformity, and falloff; do not restart only to chase intermediate prescription coverage.",\n    "Continue locally when the current trajectory is clearly improving, the next edit has a distinct mechanism, and enough eligible iterations remain to restart later.",\n    "After a harmful restart, usually try one clearly different local corrective iteration before considering another restart.",\n    "More than one restart is allowed when memory supports it; a harmful prior restart requires a clearer corrected objective rationale, not a permanent restart ban."\n  ],\n  "restart_check": [\n    "Check prior_iterations_context.history for previous restart_decision values and restart outcomes.",\n    "Check remaining_runs before choosing restart.",\n    "If no restart has been used and restart is eligible, give restart strong preference and explicitly justify any deferral.",\n    "If a restart has already been used, additional restarts remain available but must be justified by plateau, regression, persistent tradeoff tension, repeated ineffective local edits, or a corrected learned objective set."\n  ],\n  "output_rules": [\n    "Return restart_decision as \'restart\' or \'continue_without_restart\'.",\n    "If restarting, explain the memory evidence and identify which already-good clinical fronts the learned objective set is preserving.",\n    "If continuing without restart while eligible, explain why local continuation is preferred despite restart being strongly preferred in this arm."\n  ]\n}\n\n## OUTPUT CONTRACT\nReturn JSON only. Use the required top-level keys and action shapes from the output schema summary. Do not include keys outside the allowed response shape.', 'input': 'Return one valid JSON object only. Follow the output schema summary and output contract exactly. Use optimization_state.structures[*].dose_objectives only for editable objective parameters. Use optimization_state.structures[*].clinical_goals only for clinical goal status.\n\n{\n  "task": "optimizer_iteration",\n  "research_arm": {\n    "include_memory": true,\n    "include_restart": true,\n    "include_plan_data": false,\n    "include_dose_stats": false,\n    "is_llm_plan": true\n  },\n  "optimization_state": {\n    "prescription": {\n      "rx_total_dose_cgy": 4500.0,\n      "fractions": 25,\n      "rx_structure_name": "PTV4500",\n      "dose_volume_percent": 95.0\n    },\n    "summary": {\n      "TotalFunctionValue": null,\n      "num_structures": 15,\n      "num_clinical_goals": 23,\n      "num_dose_objectives": 24\n    },\n    "value_conventions": {\n      "dose_values": "cGy",\n      "dose_objectives.PercentVolume": "percent_0_to_100",\n      "clinical_goals": {\n        "DoseAtVolume": {\n          "ParameterValue": "relative_vo